    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0091" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.83/86: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-22T10:00:00+03:00">June 22, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:19 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1048. Evacuation plans which were prepared months ago are complete insofar as is
                    possible with the exception of the name of the country which would take over
                    American interests in case of evacuation. May I assume that Switzerland is
                    indicated?</p>
                <p>It is obvious that the matter should be kept secret as my first preoccupation at
                    the present moment is to avoid any action here which might smack of panic. I
                    submit that the question might be settled between Washington and Bern on the
                    understanding that instructions be not sent to the Swiss Chargé here unless and
                    until circumstances require.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
